## Pre-Test Validation

Before running any E2E tests, always verify that edited files compile cleanly.

### TypeScript / Client-Side

1. After editing any `.ts` or `.tsx` file, run `pnpm typecheck` to catch type and JSX errors before they waste time in browser-based tests.
2. The standard E2E scripts (`test:e2e`, `test:e2e:p1`, `test:e2e:flow`, `test:e2e:ready`) run `typecheck:warn` which reports errors but does not block (there are pre-existing type errors in legacy files). Use `test:e2e:fast` to skip even the warning check.
3. When `pnpm typecheck` reports errors, check whether any are in files you just edited. Pre-existing errors in files you didn't touch can be ignored for now; new errors in files you changed must be fixed before proceeding.

```bash
# Strict check (fails on any error - use after cleaning up pre-existing issues)
pnpm typecheck

# Standard E2E pipeline (warns but continues)
pnpm test:e2e

# Quick re-run (skip typecheck entirely)
pnpm test:e2e:fast
```

### Rust / Server-Side

1. After editing Rust server code in `server/src/`, run `cargo check` inside `server/` before publishing.
2. After `spacetime publish`, always regenerate client bindings with `pnpm generate`.

```bash
cd server && cargo check
spacetime publish --server local -p . --yes game
cd .. && pnpm generate
```

### Workflow Summary

| Step | Command | When |
|------|---------|------|
| Typecheck client | `pnpm typecheck` | After any `.ts`/`.tsx` edit |
| Check server | `cd server && cargo check` | After any `.rs` edit |
| Publish server | `pnpm publish:local` | After server changes |
| Regenerate bindings | `pnpm generate` | After `spacetime publish` |
| Run E2E tests | `pnpm test:e2e` | After all checks pass |
